  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "Firstly, thanks for doing this work, it was a very interesting read. \n\nIn HRM two levels of recurrence are explored, H and L modules with update. The number of module levels and cycles is a modeling hyper parameter.\n\nIn the training code, L runs 2x the number of feed forwards compared to H.\nOut of curiosity:\n - how sensitive is model performance to this hyper parameter? \n     - I.e. using a 1:1 ratio vs 1:2 vs 1:4\n - were there any results when experimenting with more levels of recurrence? \n    - I.e. High module, Middle module, Low module frequency. \n\nYou max out the benchmarks with the current configuration, so maybe this is currently being explored. I'm curious if you might have early anecdotal experimental results on it.\n\nMany thanks!",
